--- body ---
## Context

The author reports recurring /tmp growth and Disk full and asks WHERE and HOW
the harness should clean up in the work cycle. A one-shot cleanup does not
answer that request. On 2026-10-14 the author explicitly deferred this discussion
to another day while closing raids 1080 and 1089. This ticket preserves the
discussion, not authorization to implement a broad cleanup policy now.

Current mechanisms: SessionEnd/on-end.sh clears Claude session scratch;
molt sweeps recognized orphan scratch via session_scratch.py and stale
registered worktrees via worktree-gc.sh. Those mechanisms do not account for
arbitrary command/test temporary directories across runtimes. Existing
context: closed 0854 (session scratch), 0300/0303 (temporary worktree scope).

## Settled implementation

- Design 3 report-only scan/history attribution at roar and lair; Pi no-session children remain unattributed.
- Design 2 worktree-owned `.tmp/` adopted, with fail-closed citation checks; crashed/unmerged trees retain scratch.
- Session-start low-disk warning for `/tmp` and `/home`, and restic `.tmp/` exclude with host dry-run.
- Child implementation contracts: 1118 and 1119 (Blocked-by 1118), plus 1120 for bounded report profiling and honest partial attribution.

## Discussion archive

Decide an ownership/lifecycle contract for task-created temporaries. Candidate
points: source cleanup at command/test completion (finally/trap/temporary
directory context); task cleanup at roar after preserving work and evidence;
startup/molt recovery after crashes. Consider a task-specific temp root or
registry so cleanup can identify its own resources, across Codex/Claude/Pi.
Preserve live sessions, uncommitted worktrees and required review evidence.
Separate leaks in project tests from the harness's lifecycle responsibility.
No generic age-based rm of /tmp.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Record chosen lifecycle points and ownership/retention policy in the Answers and Settled implementation sections.
- [x] Define bounded implementation and verification in child tickets 1118 and 1119; 1119 depends on 1118.
- [x] Integrate and review the union of both child implementations; preserve all liveness, WIP, citation and evidence guards.

